From fac9f1eb5eaab027e479355694a7849ca20851f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Le Hoang Quyen <lehoangquyen@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:22:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-121173: Uninitialized resource in WebGL

Manual backport of patch assisted by Claude Code and originally
reviewed on https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8468008:
GL: Double clear for robust resource init on Mali and Adreno

On Mali and older Adreno drivers (the bug seems to exist on Pixel 4's
Adreno GPU as well), if an FBO attachment is drawn to, cleared to zero
(or depth 1.0, stencil 0), and then invalidated, the driver elides
subsequent robust resource initialization clears due to matching clear
values. This leaves the attachment in a DISCARD state, potentially
leaking uninitialized or recycled memory.

Implement the doubleClearForRobustInit workaround on Mali GPUs and
Adreno 6xx or older to issue a two-step clear during robust resource
initialization: first clearing to an alternate value before clearing
to the real initialization value, preventing the driver from eliding
the clear.

Bug: chromium:550489336
Change-Id: I72d8b4c66df8168d41fb763de0347c03543d8dad
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8468008
Reviewed-by: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
